# Update DEVLOG after work

After any meaningful progress in this repo, **append a dated entry** to [`adtc/docs/DEVLOG.md`](adtc/docs/DEVLOG.md) in the same session (do not wait to be asked).

## When to update

- HPC / Slurm job outcomes (success, partial, fail) with job ids and log paths when known
- Data pipeline milestones (download, normalize, mix, model download, train, merge)
- Bugs found and fixes shipped
- Gate / phase status changes
- Decisions that change the plan (skip dataset, change GPU, etc.)

Skip trivial edits (typos, comment-only) unless they affect how someone runs the project.

## Entry shape

Match existing DEVLOG style:

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD — Short title

### Outcome
One paragraph: what landed / what failed.

### What (optional bullets or tables)
Concrete paths, job names, counts, OK/FAIL.

### Next
1–5 concrete follow-ups.
```

Put new entries at the **bottom** (chronological). Do not rewrite history of older entries; add corrections as a new dated note if needed.
